  "results": [
    "Evidence remains inconclusive. Of 10 seeds evaluated, only 4 produced a test split containing any propagation-vulnerability positives; the other 6 (seeds [202, 303, 404, 505, 707, 808]) yielded undefined metrics and are excluded from every aggregate. The aggregate means (Model C raw PR-AUC 0.1473 vs Model B 0.0886, delta=+0.0587) are therefore computed over 4 seeds, not 10, and rest on 22 test positives in total. Model B and Model C produced bit-identical raw predictions on 8/10 seeds; the entire aggregate delta originates from seed(s) [101], carrying 4 test positive(s). Feature-set separation is correct and verified (B=51 features excluding borrower_propagation_exposure, C=52 features including it), so the null-on-most-seeds behaviour reflects LightGBM assigning the feature zero split gain under this target's base rate rather than a specification error. This evaluation neither demonstrates nor refutes incremental predictive value for propagation-aware exposure: the propagation-vulnerability target is too rare in the current synthetic worlds to support a directional conclusion. No causal claim is made, and nothing here generalizes to real microfinance populations.",
    "The experiment does not establish that counterfactual propagation exposure improves prediction in general.",
    "Results are specific to the synthetic worlds generated under the current NEXUS assumptions."
  ],
  "final_scientific_conclusion": "Evidence remains inconclusive. Of 10 seeds evaluated, only 4 produced a test split containing any propagation-vulnerability positives; the other 6 (seeds [202, 303, 404, 505, 707, 808]) yielded undefined metrics and are excluded from every aggregate. The aggregate means (Model C raw PR-AUC 0.1473 vs Model B 0.0886, delta=+0.0587) are therefore computed over 4 seeds, not 10, and rest on 22 test positives in total. Model B and Model C produced bit-identical raw predictions on 8/10 seeds; the entire aggregate delta originates from seed(s) [101], carrying 4 test positive(s). Feature-set separation is correct and verified (B=51 features excluding borrower_propagation_exposure, C=52 features including it), so the null-on-most-seeds behaviour reflects LightGBM assigning the feature zero split gain under this target's base rate rather than a specification error. This evaluation neither demonstrates nor refutes incremental predictive value for propagation-aware exposure: the propagation-vulnerability target is too rare in the current synthetic worlds to support a directional conclusion. No causal claim is made, and nothing here generalizes to real microfinance populations."
